% THE CAPSTONE (doc-class-capstone-road.md CP7 item 5 / CP8): a real
% upstream SATySFi 0.1 document class, `std-ja`
% (dist-v01/packages/std-ja.satyh — vendored verbatim, modulo the two
% documented math-package stand-ins its `Math` dependency needed), driving
% the FULL pipeline: V0_1 lex -> cst_v1 parse -> loader (`@require:`
% transitive resolution across annot/math/code/hyph-english/unidata/the 4
% font stand-ins/the 15 stdlib leaf packages) -> v1 lowering -> shared
% elaborate/typecheck(V0_1)/sealing -> eval -> line break -> page break ->
% PDF. Latin-only, math-free body (per the G7 single-DejaVu-face
% constraint — `std-ja`'s CJK path, `set-cjk-font`/`FontIpaEx`, is real and
% present in the class but simply never exercised by this fixture, exactly
% like the tier4 capstone's own Latin-only body never exercises stdjabook's
% CJK path).
@require: std-ja

StdJa.document (|
  title  = {SATySFi in Rust: The 0.1 Capstone},
  author = {The Vendoring Agents},
|) '<
  +StdJa.p {
    This is a real upstream SATySFi 0.1 document class, std-ja, rendered
    end to end through the Rust port: loader, elaboration, typechecking,
    evaluation, line breaking, page breaking, and PDF rendering.
  }
  +StdJa.section{Introduction}<
    +StdJa.p {
      This section proves that a sealed 0.1 module with optional-argument
      rows, closed record types, and command-argument bundles compiles and
      renders through the real pipeline.
    }
  >
  +StdJa.section{Conclusion}<
    +StdJa.p {
      The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
    }
  >
>
